    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\n\n### Module(s)\n\ncompletion, fuzzy\n\n### Description\n\n```lua\r\nrequire'mini.fuzzy'.setup {}\r\nrequire'mini.completion'.setup {\r\n  lsp_completion = {\r\n    process_items = MiniFuzzy.process_lsp_items,\r\n  },\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nWhen typing something that should fuzzy-match, I get no results.\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.8.1\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Open some source code (Rust in this case)\r\n2. Type something that should match exactly, eg `std::coll` for `std::collections`\r\n3. Type something that matches fuzzily, eg `std::cct`\n\n### Expected behavior\n\n`std::cct` matches `std::collections`\n\n### Actual behavior\n\nNo results.",
