        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "~~It seems something is overriding the config at some point. This causes things to break when `process_items2` is set to `nil`. Completions work if set to `MiniFuzzy.process_lsp_items`, but still no fuzzy matching. :(~~\r\n\r\n```diff\r\n--- a/lua/mini/completion.lua\r\n+++ b/lua/mini/completion.lua\r\n@@ -513,7 +513,7 @@ MiniCompletion.completefunc_lsp = function(findstart, base)\r\n       -- Response can be `CompletionList` with 'items' field or `CompletionItem[]`\r\n       local items = H.table_get(response, { 'items' }) or response\r\n       if type(items) ~= 'table' then return {} end\r\n-      items = config.lsp_completion.process_items(items, base)\r\n+      items = config.lsp_completion.process_items2(items, base)\r\n       return H.lsp_completion_response_items_to_complete_items(items, client_id)\r\n     end)\r\n \r\n```\r\n\r\nSetting `process_items = function () end` actually errors out too, so I guess there is no bug here. I'm not sure why fuzzy matching isn't working then, maybe it's a server issue? But rust-analyzer apparently fuzzy-matches server-side.",
